  "arithmetic_and_order": [
    "Generated baseline/candidate core diff changes only history header selection and local QR body to a shared call. Candidate header retains original history_get/history_put code verbatim and replaces the history loop with the same shared call at packed mode1.",
    "For each pivot: read a and b; compute same hypot; reject nonfinite h before stores; skip same n-j span for zero h; compute c=a/h and s=b/h from unrounded h; store diagonal and read it back before the finite check. Each trailing update reads old r and v, stores c*r+s*v, stores c*v-s*r to x, then checks stored coefficient and x in the original short-circuit order.",
    "No staging or delayed write; every six-byte rounding point remains. Local double assignment keeps binary64 storage. Packed overflow to infinity is detected immediately by readback. Failure leaves the same partial-update boundary and returns-1.",
    "Changing local p from int to unsigned is harmless within valid extents. Integrated n17 local requires153 doubles and row17; n34 history requires595 six-byte entries and row34. No public shape expansion or claim for arbitrary oversized n is introduced.",
    "void* conversion returns to actual declared double or history_store type only on its matching mode branch. Double alignment is inherited; packed alignment is1 and get/put use memcpy, without misaligned integer/double loads. R and x remain disjoint and externally valid for the call.",
    "No new persistent data, scratch copy, cache, ownership, prior, evidence duplication, sample-order or physical-state change. rebuild invalidates before factor mutation; append/ingest/stream failure invalidation is unchanged; host quarantine rejects later query, fit and advance after late history failure. Calls still require serialized callers; leases are not thread/interrupt synchronization."
  ],
